      "title": "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b63bb02a-f207-500e-99cd-a59750a57f2a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\text{det}(M)$, if\n$M=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -9 \\\\ 10 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & -9 \\\\ 10 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 2-(-9)\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =-8-(-90) \\\\  & =82\\end{aligned}\n$$",
